      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mather%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was built in 1917 by Picklands‑Mather of Cincinnati, Ohio, who opened a coal mine called Mather Collieries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://greenescenemagazine.com/i-love-this-place-mather/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During its 46‑year history, the mine produced an estimated 33.4 million tons of coal.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.oocities.org/mathercoalpa/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mather’s streets were paved and tree‑lined, with tidy one‑ and two‑story homes that had indoor plumbing—an early model for a coal town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://greenescenemagazine.com/i-love-this-place-mather/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town square featured a six‑sided gazebo, nicknamed the Liars Den, surrounded by a church, post office, recreation building, theater, and a drug store.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://greenescenemagazine.com/i-love-this-place-mather/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Mine safety was a priority; workers knew methane’s danger and the town’s design reflected modern standards for the era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
